# printImage(a fully transparent 16 x 2 TYPE_INT_ARGB image)   -- body only
# Alpha below 128 is treated as WHITE. Without that rule a transparent PNG logo prints
# as a solid black box, because its RGB channels are all zero.
1B 61 01                  # ESC a 1     centre
1D 76 30 00 02 00 02 00   # GS v 0 0    2 bytes wide, 2 rows
00 00                     # row 0: no dots
00 00                     # row 1: no dots
1B 61 00                  # ESC a 0     back to left
